      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The 100MB limit is keeping a lot of currently PC-only content off of iOS and Android entirely by itself. Unlike other runtime optimization for ARM which is tractable, download size optimization has an impassable and absolute limit. If you’re already heavily optimizing for download size on PC and you’re over 300 MB (densely packed full of content) It tends to be impossible to get below 110 MB for mobile, even if it can run just fine with well-managed batching/culling that keeps draw calls low. Unity only lets you downscale textures so far, and mesh already compresses as efficiently as it can.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
